      "source_number": "182",
      "task": "Infer the increased train speed over the final 120 km from a 15-minute delay and a 1.2 speed factor.",
      "solution": "Let the scheduled speed be v>0 km/h. The remaining scheduled time is 120/v h, the actual running time is 120/(1.2v) h, and the time saved is 15/60=1/4 h. Thus 120/v-120/(1.2v)=20/v=1/4, so v=80 km/h and the actual running speed is 1.2v=96 km/h. Check: scheduled time 1.5 h, actual time 1.25 h, difference 0.25 h. The requested speed is not the scheduled 80 km/h.",
