      "source_number": "183",
      "task": "Solve two equations graphically using y=6/x and respectively y=x-1 and y=x+3.",
      "solution": "Both equations require x!=0. For 6/x=x-1, multiply by x to get x^2-x-6=(x-3)(x+2)=0, hence x=-2 or 3. Graph intersections are (-2,-3) and (3,2). For 6/x=x+3, get x^2+3x-6=0, hence x=(-3-sqrt(33))/2 or (-3+sqrt(33))/2, approximately -4.372281323 and 1.372281323. Corresponding y coordinates are (3-sqrt(33))/2 and (3+sqrt(33))/2, approximately -1.372281323 and 4.372281323. These independent algebraic checks identify the intended graph intersections, but they are not evidence of constructing or reading a graph.",
